  "cards": [
    { "dot": "cyan", "title": "Security posture", "items": ["Loopback-only bind (127.0.0.1) with a DNS-rebinding-safe Host/Origin guard on every HTTP request and the WS upgrade; the server is .unref()'d and never keeps the process alive.", "Every /files response carries Content-Security-Policy: sandbox allow-scripts allow-downloads (opaque origin — the document can never reach /api or the WS endpoint same-origin) plus X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff.", "Containment mirrors /output: decode-after-strip, NUL reject, realpathSync both sides, regular files only — traversal, symlink hop, escape, and missing file are all the SAME uniform 404 that never leaks existence. An empty root allowlist (the default) serves nothing."] },
    { "dot": "rose", "title": "Floor control", "items": ["The TUI and the browser share one agent: pi.on(\"input\") IS the gate — the mutex-controller returns the InputEventResult that allows or blocks each submission, and agent_settled releases the floor.", "A suppressed interactive (TUI) submission surfaces a ui.notify warning instead of silently stalling; web-side blocks are already visible in the browser.", "Outbound frames QUEUE while the WS reconnects so a HITL answer is never lost; idleTimeout 0 keeps a silent HITL gate alive while the user thinks for minutes."] },
    { "dot": "emerald", "title": "/files + webui:open contract", "items": ["Rendered views (webui:render) strip scripts; /files serves FULL-FIDELITY HTML (e.g. archify diagrams whose product IS the inline JS runtime) as a top-level browser tab, not a shell view.", "webui:open {path, view?, title?} rides the shared pi.events bus; the handler validates against the SAME root allowlist + containment core as the route, then announces a clickable URL via ui.notify (percent-encoded per segment).", "archify emits webui:open after every successful archify_render / archify_delta — an optional-chain emit: no webui present, or a path outside its roots, is a silent no-op. webui imports nothing from archify and vice versa; the string-literal channel is the whole contract."] }
  ]
